abstract: >-
  Bash program, also an extension of the GitHub CLI, that pulls, commits, pushes, resets and clones
  every git repository under a folder, several at a time, with one line of report for each repository
  that changed or needs attention. It never forces a push and never loses work: a conflict is undone
  at once, nothing is committed unless asked for, a push waits for one confirmation, and a reset
  keeps the previous commit under a reference of its own.
